WEBVTT

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:15.040
<i>DOKI - Chihiro</i>

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:15.040
<i>DOKI</i>

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:21.870
<b>fukigenna tenki moyou ga nori utsutteta aitsu</b>

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:21.870
<b>不機嫌な天気模様が乗り移ってたアイツ</b>

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:21.870
<b>That fellow was affected by bad weather</b>

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:28.040
<b>nanda! chotto naname ni sora wo miteta dake ka</b>

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:28.040
<b>なんだ！　ちょっとナナメに空を見てただけか</b>

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:28.040
<b>What! He's only squinting at the sky</b>

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:29.630
<b>shiritai (misetai)</b>

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:29.630
<b>知りたい（見せたい）</b>

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:29.630
<b>I want to know (I want to see)</b>

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:31.210
<b>wakaritai (wakaranai)</b>

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:31.210
<b>解りたい（解らない）</b>

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:31.210
<b>I want to understand (I can't understand)</b>

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:32.800
<b>nakitai (nakenai)</b>

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:32.800
<b>泣きたい（泣けない）</b>

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:32.800
<b>I want to cry (I can't cry)</b>

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:34.380
<b>soredemo</b>

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:34.380
<b>それでも</b>

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:34.380
<b>Even so,</b>

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:35.970
<b>shikatanai (kubomanai)</b>

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:35.970
<b>仕方ない（凹まない）</b>

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:35.970
<b>It can't be helped (Not feeling depressed)</b>

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:37.590
<b>itakunai (youkumonai)</b>

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:37.590
<b>痛くない（痒くもない）</b>

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:37.590
<b>It doesn't hurt (It doesn't itch)</b>

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:38.970
<b>kowashitai (kowaretai)</b>

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:38.970
<b>壊したい（壊れたい）</b>

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:38.970
<b>I want to break (I want to be broken)</b>

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:42.640
<b>yuzurenai omoi nara</b>

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:42.640
<b>譲れない思いなら</b>

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:42.640
<b>I don't want to surrender these feelings</b>

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:48.400
<b>chiratsuku kiiro shingou mushishite</b>

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:48.400
<b>ちらつく黄色信号　無視して</b>

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:48.400
<b>Just ignore that flashing yellow signal</b>

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:54.030
<b>kou kakudo de joushou chuu kokoro no flying saucer</b>

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:54.030
<b>高角度で上昇中　心のflying saucer</b>

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:54.030
<b>The flying saucer in my heart is rising at a sharp angle</b>

00:00:54.030 --> 00:01:00.870
<b>nakanaka sunao ni nan nai himitsu no tobira ni keri irete!</b>

00:00:54.030 --> 00:01:00.870
<b>なかなか素直になんない秘密のトビラに蹴り入れて！</b>

00:00:54.030 --> 00:01:00.870
<b>It kicks open that dishonest, secret door</b>

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:04.080
<b>chuugaeri de mata modotte kuru yo</b>

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:04.080
<b>宙返りでまた戻ってくるよ</b>

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:04.080
<b>Do a loop-the-loop and return once more {Loop-the-Loop is the title of this song}</b>

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:12.500
<b>sakaraenai jiryoku mitai na omoi yo todoke!</b>

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:12.500
<b>逆らえない磁力みたいな思いよ　届け！</b>

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:12.500
<b>Convey those seemingly irresistable magnetic feelings to you!</b>

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:20.180
<b>omote no kādo de shoubu shinai nande</b>

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:20.180
<b>表のカードで勝負しないなんで</b>

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:20.180
<b>You can't use a face card to decide the victory.</b>

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:23.060
<b>dare no tame no moraru?</b>

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:23.060
<b>誰のためのモラル？</b>

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:23.060
<b>Whose morals are those?</b>

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:36.950
Motto To LOVE-Ru 19

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:36.950
<u>Yami's Clinic</u>

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:55.720
What was that?

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:58.180
Yami?

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:02.390
What happened? Did you trip? {TLC: Fall?}{trip up}

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:05.430
Yuuki Rito.

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:11.400
I'm sorry.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:12.650
Don't worry about it.

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:18.030
But you sure like reading books, eh?

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:24.410
There are a lot of books here. I really enjoy them.

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:30.040
How unusual to see you in a place like this.

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:33.590
Well, I was just checking something up.

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:35.090
That's good. {TLC}{Good for you}

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:38.340
You should read more books.

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:41.840
If you did, you would be more intelligent.

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:44.640
You're right...

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:46.850
Here.

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:55.610
W-Wait!

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:05.330
What happened?

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:09.620
It's... none of your business.

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:12.040
Even though you say that...

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:13.960
Hot!

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:16.670
You have a really high temperature!

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:20.800
It's... nothing.

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:27.890
What are you{fscx200}-

00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:32.900
We need to go and see Mikado-sensei. I'll take you there right now. {TLC}

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:35.610
It's not really necessary.

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:41.070
Yami!

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:42.530
I need to hurry!

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:44.530
<b>Infirmary{GUESSLATED -masat}{good guess}{gamma- i \an8}</b>

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:44.530
Mikado-sensei!

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:46.330
She's not here!

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:48.080
Damn...

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:50.330
What's up?

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:54.130
Lala, Oshizu-chan... Do you know where Mikado-sensei is?

00:03:54.130 --> 00:03:55.250
I haven't seen her.

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:58.090
If you're looking for Mikado-sensei, she took the day off.

00:03:58.090 --> 00:04:02.220
She had to attend to an emergency until late last night, so she's sleeping in today. {TLC: The first half of this sentence}

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:05.930
As usual, this school is so casual! {TLC: Lax/casual/informal?}

00:04:05.930 --> 00:04:08.140
What's wrong with Yami-chan?

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:09.220
She's sick.

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:12.180
Eh? Then let's go to Mikado-sensei's house to see her. {TLC}

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:20.610
Rito! Hurry!

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:21.900
Yeah.

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:27.030
Wait a bit, Yami!

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:30.120
Mikado-sensei!

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:36.250
Oh my. What's the matter?

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:39.840
Why are you dressed like that?!

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:41.550
I've been sleeping up till now. {TLC}

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:44.380
Sensei! Yami-chan's...

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:51.770
I see.

00:04:52.390 --> 00:04:55.230
This isn't a normal cold. {TLC kaze byouki}

00:04:55.230 --> 00:04:57.270
It's a special case to this girl.

00:04:57.650 --> 00:05:00.690
Sensei, will Yami-chan be all right?

00:05:00.690 --> 00:05:01.820
Of course!

00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:05.150
As long as you're not dead, no matter what illness you have, I can cure it. {TLC}

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:09.160
Amazing. As expected of the universal doctor. {TLC: Universal doctor?}

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:10.370
Yuuki-kun?

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:13.200
I need to take her clothes off, so give us a hand.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:17.880
Usually it's Oshizu-chan's job, but today she's not here. {TLC: Usually, it's Oshizu-chan's job?}

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:19.080
So... Hurry.

00:05:19.590 --> 00:05:21.380
W-Why{fscx200}-

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:25.970
In order to heal this girl faster, she should be put in the healing capsule.

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:28.800
Her clothes will interfere inside...{TLC}

00:05:36.770 --> 00:05:39.940
Hold her properly now...

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:44.150
This is all for medical purposes...

00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:48.610
What's the matter? You shouldn't be so nervous over something like this.

00:05:54.870 --> 00:05:56.410
He's no good after all. {TLC: Guess here}

00:05:56.410 --> 00:05:57.410
Sensei!

00:05:57.710 --> 00:06:01.170
I'll help you!

00:06:01.790 --> 00:06:03.000
Take that! And that!

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:06.220
Ah Lala-chan, you're so quick!

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:08.720
All right, help me move her.

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:11.890
It'll be fine now.

00:06:11.890 --> 00:06:13.720
Leave the rest to me.

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:15.270
Yep!

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:18.810
Rito, let's go and buy Yami-chan some "get well soon" presents! {TLC}

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:35.740
You're awake, Yami-chan.

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:38.330
Doctor Mikado.

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:42.330
Your body has weakened quite a bit. {TLC}

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:46.050
After all, you're on Earth, where the environment is unsuitable. {TLC}

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:47.590
Your weariness will catch up to you. {TLC}

00:06:49.590 --> 00:06:51.930
Why am I here?

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:54.930
You should thank Yuuki-kun.

00:06:56.220 --> 00:07:00.270
He carried you all the way here. {TLC}

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:03.110
He was dripping with sweat too.

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:14.410
Oh. Are you all right now?

00:07:14.410 --> 00:07:15.330
Yes.

00:07:20.370 --> 00:07:22.080
I cannot understand.

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:25.210
Why would he help his enemy...

00:07:25.500 --> 00:07:28.380
Maybe he doesn't see it that way...

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:35.760
Please pay your medical fee with Earth currency. {TLC}

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:37.100
Understood.

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:41.850
We're back!

00:07:41.850 --> 00:07:43.940
We got you some taiyaki to wish you well!

00:07:43.940 --> 00:07:45.730
Stop pulling me!

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:55.950
I-I didn't mean to...

00:07:56.450 --> 00:07:57.580
Just die!

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:02.670
Rito!

00:08:02.670 --> 00:08:04.920
Please don't do this in my house!

00:08:10.970 --> 00:08:16.640
Motto To LOVE-Ru 20

00:08:10.970 --> 00:08:16.640
<u>The Antagonist</u>

00:08:10.970 --> 00:08:12.510
Run-chan!

00:08:12.510 --> 00:08:14.260
I saw it on TV!

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:17.970
You're going to be on Magical Girl Kyouko, right? Amazing! {TLC: Kyouko?}

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:23.640
How nice for you to get on Magical Girl Kyouko... Nice! Nice! Nice!

00:08:20.140 --> 00:08:21.520
Yeah...

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:23.640
Oh, I see!

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:27.440
Is Magical Girl Kyouko that special effects show? {TLC: special}

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:30.150
And you sing the ending theme, right?

00:08:30.150 --> 00:08:31.780
Amazing, Run-run!

00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:35.360
It's like you've become a true musical artist.

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:37.280
I guess...

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:40.330
All right, I'll see you later.

00:08:40.830 --> 00:08:41.870
Run.

00:08:42.450 --> 00:08:43.870
I'll be looking forward to it.

00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:45.830
A-All right.{added "Y- " -masat}

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:51.380
I'm happy that Rito-kun said that,

00:08:52.210 --> 00:08:56.260
but the truth is, I'm not really interested...

00:09:13.990 --> 00:09:15.740
Playing the role of the villain...

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:19.700
Besides, why do I have to wear such embarrassing clothes?

00:09:20.780 --> 00:09:23.750
Run-chuan! You're so cute!

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:27.170
Kyouko-sama is here!

00:09:27.170 --> 00:09:27.920
W-What're you{fscx200}-

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:30.380
Kyouko-chan, I'll leave today up to you. {TLC}

00:09:30.790 --> 00:09:34.050
All right, Director. Please guide me well. {TLC}

00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:36.840
Kirisaki Kyouko.

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:39.640
What's with her? Why are they flattering her so much?

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:42.470
I'm also a high school idol, you know.

00:09:42.470 --> 00:09:45.140
I'll be watching carefully behind the camera! {TLC no idea...}

00:09:45.140 --> 00:09:47.100
I'll leave it to you.

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:49.270
I have no idea what you're saying, Director.

00:09:49.610 --> 00:09:53.280
Let's start!{seems like some bits are missing here -masat}{I have no idea... slang speech...}{gamma- too short for what's being said what should we put here? *wishes he was a master at japanese at times like these}

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:55.780
Well, it <i>is</i>  her program.

00:09:55.780 --> 00:09:58.990
And I'm just a side character. {TLC: side char?}

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:02.120
<b>Magical Kyouko</b>

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:02.740
Get set... Action! {TLC}

00:10:02.120 --> 00:10:02.200
<b>Magical Kyouko</b>

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:02.280
<b>Magical Kyouko</b>

00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:02.410
<b>Magical Kyouko</b>

00:10:02.410 --> 00:10:02.490
<b>Magical Kyouko</b>

00:10:02.490 --> 00:10:02.580
<b>Magical Kyouko</b>

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:02.740
<b>Magical Kyouko</b>

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:02.870
<b>Magical Kyouko</b>

00:10:02.870 --> 00:10:02.990
<b>Magical Kyouko</b>

00:10:02.990 --> 00:10:03.120
<b>Magical Kyouko</b>

00:10:06.120 --> 00:10:08.290
So... this is the end for you.

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:10.580
Pierre Ogi, prepare yourself. {TLC: Names}

00:10:11.960 --> 00:10:15.420
My cute ideal attack has been foiled. {TLC wtf sentence}

00:10:15.420 --> 00:10:17.470
Damn you, Magical Girl Kyouko!

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:19.680
Retreat, Pierre Ogi.

00:10:20.470 --> 00:10:22.640
You guys are no match against Kyouko.

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:24.220
You are{fscx200}-

00:10:24.220 --> 00:10:25.810
Yes, Usas!

00:10:31.690 --> 00:10:37.740
I'm the boss of the evil organisation of Usas, Blue Metallia.

00:10:38.490 --> 00:10:42.200
Now that I am present, things will be different!

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:42.990
Magical Girl Kyouko!

00:10:42.990 --> 00:10:45.620
Cut! Cut! Cut!

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:46.750
That's not good enough!

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:50.580
You have to laugh evilly whilst saying it!

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:52.080
All right.

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:55.000
Why it is a yes to Kyouko and a no to me?

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:01.760
We're going to take a 30 minute break.

00:11:08.980 --> 00:11:10.730
I wanna go home already...

00:11:11.350 --> 00:11:12.440
Run-chan.

00:11:12.860 --> 00:11:13.810
Good work. {TLC otsukaresama}

00:11:14.190 --> 00:11:15.320
Kyouko.

00:11:15.650 --> 00:11:19.190
Your acting just now, was very appealing!

00:11:20.570 --> 00:11:22.990
Was it?

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:26.700
What's up? You don't look well.

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:30.660
As you can see, I'm tired.

00:11:30.660 --> 00:11:32.880
So, let's eat this together?

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:35.920
Cream-filled pastry from Misora?!

00:11:36.460 --> 00:11:40.550
Yes. You wrote in your "Run Run Diary" that these were your favourite, right?

00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:46.220
You've read my blog...

00:11:49.850 --> 00:11:51.520
I've been following it for a while.

00:11:53.560 --> 00:11:56.360
I'm your fan after all, Run-chan.

00:11:57.980 --> 00:12:01.740
I have a complete collection of your CDs, from when you first debuted. {gamma - shortened as it was very redundant to say "first started since your debut"}

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:02.450
No way...

00:12:02.450 --> 00:12:04.530
No, it's true.

00:12:05.280 --> 00:12:10.750
Actually, when work isn't going so well, and I'm feeling down,

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:13.830
I've always got encouragement by listening to your songs.

00:12:15.330 --> 00:12:20.460
So when I found out that you were going to appear on this show,

00:12:20.460 --> 00:12:22.340
I was really happy.

00:12:24.340 --> 00:12:27.180
So, let's open it and eat!

00:12:28.310 --> 00:12:29.890
Sure...

00:12:31.890 --> 00:12:35.690
Kirisaki Kyouko... is actually a nice person. {TLC Kiisaki/kisaki}

00:12:35.690 --> 00:12:39.570
And I've only been thinking badly of her.

00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:41.360
I feel a little guilty.

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:43.740
What's the matter?

00:12:43.740 --> 00:12:46.570
Nothing. It's nothing.

00:12:46.570 --> 00:12:47.740
Run-chan?

00:12:47.740 --> 00:12:49.120
Run-chan!

00:12:49.410 --> 00:12:52.620
Please autograph my body! {Please autograph on his body?}

00:12:52.620 --> 00:12:54.330
H-Headmaster?

00:12:54.330 --> 00:12:56.170
W-Who are you?

00:12:57.750 --> 00:12:59.840
This one is cute too!

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:02.380
Ouch...

00:13:02.380 --> 00:13:05.130
No! No!

00:13:05.760 --> 00:13:07.140
You beast!

00:13:07.140 --> 00:13:08.600
Kiss~

00:13:13.140 --> 00:13:15.520
Eh?!

00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:17.900
Pervert!

00:13:25.280 --> 00:13:27.240
That's not CG...

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:29.660
They're... real flames?!

00:13:30.450 --> 00:13:32.240
Kyouko...

00:13:32.240 --> 00:13:37.080
P-Perhaps... You're an alien?

00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:40.880
N-No! T-That was magic!

00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:43.920
S-See, it was magic. I'm really good at magic.

00:13:43.920 --> 00:13:45.260
L-Look...

00:13:45.260 --> 00:13:47.930
There's no need to hide it.

00:13:49.140 --> 00:13:52.390
I am also from Planet Memorze.

00:13:54.390 --> 00:13:57.600
You're half Flame-jin and half Earthling?

00:13:57.600 --> 00:14:02.270
Yes... I've been able to emit heat and flames ever since I was born.

00:14:02.940 --> 00:14:09.570
This show is for me to develop my ability. The producer planned it for me specifically.

00:14:09.570 --> 00:14:13.410
The producer is actually an alien as well.

00:14:13.910 --> 00:14:18.790
But on Earth, no one knows about the existence of aliens yet.

00:14:18.790 --> 00:14:21.880
The other employees are told that this is a specially taught magic. {TLC}

00:14:25.710 --> 00:14:30.640
Hey. Can I write about today's events on my blog?

00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:33.060
Eh!? You can't!

00:14:33.060 --> 00:14:34.890
Not that...

00:14:36.220 --> 00:14:39.440
About how I've become friends with you, Kyouko-chan.

00:14:43.940 --> 00:14:47.070
For now, let's swap e-mail addresses, OK? {TLC swop email?}

00:14:47.070 --> 00:14:48.030
Sure.

00:14:55.950 --> 00:15:00.830
Motto To LOVE-Ru 21

00:14:55.950 --> 00:15:00.830
<u>A Strange Haruna-chan</u>

00:15:07.960 --> 00:15:11.640
A stray dog? I wonder where it came from.

00:15:14.350 --> 00:15:16.930
Why are you barking like that?

00:15:23.650 --> 00:15:25.150
Morning, Haruna!

00:15:26.150 --> 00:15:29.240
Yes! Good morning!

00:15:30.900 --> 00:15:34.450
It is wonderful to see you two looking so well!

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:37.160
Haruna, you look lively too!

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:38.250
Yes!

00:15:38.830 --> 00:15:42.210
Haruna-chan... Compared to how she usually is...

00:15:42.210 --> 00:15:43.580
Ha-ru-na!

00:15:43.580 --> 00:15:44.420
Yes?

00:15:46.170 --> 00:15:47.920
Morning!

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:50.470
You look really lively today.

00:15:53.640 --> 00:15:55.430
It tickles!

00:15:56.050 --> 00:15:58.180
If it's like that, I'll return the favour!

00:16:01.140 --> 00:16:02.060
What's wrong?

00:16:02.060 --> 00:16:03.980
Haruna would do something like that...

00:16:03.980 --> 00:16:05.810
Looks fun!

00:16:05.810 --> 00:16:07.520
I'm joining in!

00:16:11.110 --> 00:16:14.740
You guys! Can you stop being so noisy so early in the morning?!

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:18.950
Even you, Class Rep Sairenji-san. What were you thinking?!

00:16:18.950 --> 00:16:21.160
Kotegawa.

00:16:21.160 --> 00:16:23.960
All right, Yui-san can join in too.

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:26.840
What are you doing?!

00:16:26.840 --> 00:16:28.250
Stop it!

00:16:31.260 --> 00:16:34.840
Ah! How cute. What is this?

00:16:36.760 --> 00:16:38.760
Isn't this cute?

00:16:40.310 --> 00:16:44.310
Don't tell me, that's... my...

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:47.360
Give it back!

00:16:47.360 --> 00:16:49.610
What is that called?

00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:51.820
It's a bra! {TLC: Does she say bra?}

00:16:51.820 --> 00:16:53.530
You're wearing one too, right?

00:16:59.030 --> 00:17:00.790
Ah! I really am!

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:02.450
Hey, Haruna...

00:17:02.450 --> 00:17:04.120
Aren't you overdoing this?

00:17:04.830 --> 00:17:06.080
Really?

00:17:06.080 --> 00:17:08.130
You're really strange today, Haruna.

00:17:08.460 --> 00:17:12.510
Haruna-dono... Did she have a personality like that?

00:17:12.510 --> 00:17:14.300
Hmm...

00:17:14.300 --> 00:17:16.130
There's something a bit weird about her.

00:17:23.020 --> 00:17:26.350
Haruna-chan is being really strange today.

00:17:26.350 --> 00:17:30.570
She's not the usual Haruna-chan. What happened?

00:17:47.120 --> 00:17:48.290
Rito-san.

00:17:53.210 --> 00:17:54.840
Sairenji.

00:17:57.720 --> 00:18:01.640
What's up? Did you need me for something?

00:18:02.600 --> 00:18:08.650
Yes. Um... There's something I need to tell you.

00:18:09.310 --> 00:18:10.980
Tell me?

00:18:10.980 --> 00:18:11.900
Yes.

00:18:16.320 --> 00:18:19.070
Um...

00:18:30.920 --> 00:18:32.040
I...

00:18:32.920 --> 00:18:34.300
...actually...

00:18:37.340 --> 00:18:40.090
...like you.

00:18:41.890 --> 00:18:44.390
Wait a sec! What did you just say?!

00:18:44.970 --> 00:18:46.930
I like you!

00:18:50.150 --> 00:18:51.190
Like...

00:18:51.520 --> 00:18:53.690
Haruna-chan likes me?!

00:18:55.230 --> 00:19:00.700
It happened! The dream I longed for has finally come true!

00:19:03.200 --> 00:19:06.410
Yes. Me too...

00:19:07.790 --> 00:19:10.750
Actually, I also{fscx200}-

00:19:20.840 --> 00:19:24.300
Stop it! He's barking so much. {TLC}

00:19:30.940 --> 00:19:33.650
A dog!

00:19:33.650 --> 00:19:35.650
Oshizu-chan?

00:19:36.900 --> 00:19:38.400
Don't come near me!

00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:42.030
I'm sorry!

00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:52.040
Do whatever you can to get rid of the dog! {TLC}

00:19:52.040 --> 00:19:56.750
I dislike dogs the most!

00:19:56.750 --> 00:19:59.010
What actually happened? {Barely audible, if timer can't hear this, delete}

00:19:59.340 --> 00:20:01.720
Oshizu-chan was inside Haruna-chan?

00:20:03.050 --> 00:20:04.140
Sorry!

00:20:04.760 --> 00:20:07.720
Why are you in your spirit form today?

00:20:07.720 --> 00:20:12.310
My body is undergoing maintenance at Mikado-sensei's place right now. {TLC}

00:20:12.770 --> 00:20:17.320
When I was wandering the streets, a wild dog chased me.

00:20:19.480 --> 00:20:20.860
Help!

00:20:21.240 --> 00:20:23.990
It's a dog!

00:20:27.830 --> 00:20:34.000
When I was running away, I ran into Haruna in front at the school gates. {TLC}

00:20:35.380 --> 00:20:36.710
It's a dog!

00:20:39.300 --> 00:20:42.220
So then, you possessed her? {TLC}

00:20:42.220 --> 00:20:48.760
I wasn't going to stay long at first, but it was interesting, so...

00:20:48.760 --> 00:20:50.810
Honestly... You caused so much trouble...

00:20:51.560 --> 00:20:55.520
Is it true? You used my body to confess to Yuuki-kun...

00:20:56.270 --> 00:20:57.690
Um...

00:21:00.110 --> 00:21:02.280
That was strange.

00:21:02.780 --> 00:21:06.870
Why did I feel like doing something like that at the time?

00:21:08.280 --> 00:21:13.330
I didn't really plan on doing it. Sorry, Haruna-san. {TLC}

00:21:19.210 --> 00:21:20.630
Um...

00:21:24.380 --> 00:21:27.840
Your face has gone red. What's the matter?

00:21:27.840 --> 00:21:31.970
Haruna-chan's gone back to how she used to be.

00:21:31.970 --> 00:21:35.440
I'm relieved... But it's a shame... {TLC}

00:21:36.770 --> 00:21:38.350
Let's see...

00:21:38.350 --> 00:21:39.690
Stop it, Risa!

00:21:41.110 --> 00:21:43.440
What are you doing?!

00:21:43.740 --> 00:21:45.820
Yep. Haruna-chan's back to normal.

00:21:45.820 --> 00:21:47.320
Good, good!

00:21:47.320 --> 00:21:49.410
It's not good! Stop it!

00:21:49.410 --> 00:21:51.990
How interesting! Let me join in!

00:21:51.990 --> 00:21:54.370
I want to join in too!

